worker: Do not restart a finished looping call

oslo.service's threading backend wakes wait() before it releases the
loop's thread, and refuses to start that looping call again until it
has, so PeriodicWorker.start() straight after stop() and wait() could
raise RuntimeError. wait() now drops the finished loop for a new one.

The oslo.service side is fixed separately; this keeps neutron working
with releases that predate that fix.

